  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Jamil vs State on 21 March, 2024 Author: Praveer Bhatnagar Bench: Praveer Bhatnagar [2024:Rj-Jp:11523] High Court Of Judicature For Rajasthan Bench At Jaipur S.B. Criminal Revision Petition No. 858/2005 Jamil son of Niwaj Khan, R/o Kutukpur, Police Station Nagar, District Bharatpur. At presnt in Sub-jail, Deeg, District Bharatpur. ----Petitione Versus The State of Rajasthan through Pp ----Respondent For Petitioner(s) : Mr.Dharmendra Choudhary For Respondent(s) : Mr.Chitragupt Chopra, Public Prosecutor Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Praveer Bhatnagar Order Date of Reserve :: 31/01/2024 Date of Pronouncement :: 21/03/2024 Reportable:",
    "facts": "The petitioner filed an appeal against the order of the trial Court and but the Appellate Court dismissed appeal of the petitioner vide order dated 30.08.2005.",
    "arguments": "4. Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that the Courts below erred in passing the order. He submits that the Court below have not taken into consideration that provisions of Section 13(2) [2024:RJ-JP:11523] (3 of 10) [CRLR-858/2005] of the Act of 1954 have not been complied with. He further submits that as per the prosecution story, analyst report was sent to the petitioner through registered post on 17.04.1996, however, neither acknowledgment nor any evidence was produced before the Courts below showing that registered post was received by the petitioner. He also submits that the Court below has not taken into consideration the statement of Sher Mohammad (DW-1) that petitioner was not engaged in business of sale of milk. 5. Learned counsel submits that the Appellate Court has not taken into consideration that the trial Court has convicted the petitioner after adopting the summary trial, whereas trial Court ought to have conducted warrant trial. He further submits that Prosecution Sanction, given by Chief Medical Officer, was given in a routine way and was without application of mind. In view of the above, learned counsel for the petitioner prays that the orders dated 30.08.2005 and 15.01.1998 may be [LEAKAGE_MASK] and [LEAKAGE_MASK]."
  },
