      {
        "annotation_id": "0766fa0c99014695a2cb83e314ae0e43_34",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "If one looks into various judgements of this Court, it emerges that revisional jurisdiction can be invoked where the decisions under challenge are grossly erroneous, there is no compliance with the provisions of law, the finding recorded is"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "032339233d484964b8fce7dcf74a6cd4_35",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "These are not exhaustive classes, but merely indicative."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "afa028998a604cd9a5665ff33874e5ae_36",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Each case would have to be determined on its own merits."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "91446ae3566640c38413e0b0160218de_37",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "9. Thus in the light of the law laid down, this Court has to see whether there is patent illegality or error of jurisdiction and findings recorded by the courts below are perverse and against the evidence.\n10. I have gone through the Judgme"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "626d7ef88ccf48699daede6199b28f9a_38",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Sheer non"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "1975b7c49e8440eca9b90a7b989725a3_39",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "-support of independent eyewitnesses is not enough to negate the testimony of the food inspector particularly in the absence of any specific allegation of previous enmity with the accused- petitioner."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "c39a5d357d9f4a14a3cf72ce1ca9d8e9_40",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "11. As far as the non-compliance of Section 13 (2) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (for short \"the Act of 2006\") is concerned, it is evident that after filing the analyst report a copy of the same was sent to the accused through "
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "70c16810f5bb40598304e3a687cb39ad_41",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The postal receipt indicating the address is enough to presume that the accused received the Food analyst report."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "aaad3449c68c44bbbb75d9c33b01065d_42",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Under Section 114 of the Indian Evidence Act read with Section 27 of the General Clauses Act, the Court may presume that the accused duly received the report."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "250a9a60e3d04aef9dfaf3f519792e64_43",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "12. The Apex Court in the case of C.C. Alavi Haji Vs. Palapetty Muhammed & Anr."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "007ea3e22afa48d28a6ae521dc85d6f6_44",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n[(2007) 6 SCC 555] opined that Section 27 of the General Clauses Act gives rise to a presumption that service of notice has been effected when it is sent to the correct address by registered post unless and until the contrary is proved by "
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "2ffce7c755f74d8ebb5cd777cb5a8b59_45",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "A similar view was taken by the Court in the case of M/s. Madan & Co. Vs. Wazir Jaivir Chand [(1989) 1 SCC 264]."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "509e937876a647ce841899fa77d7954e_46",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nIn this case, the Apex Court, while dealing with whether the duty of the landlord was complete by sending of notice with reference to the presumption under Section 27 of General Clauses Act, held that once there is a proper tender of the d"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "6c701f932e7c4adf8c86750412160c88_47",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Similarly, in the case of Parimal Vs. Veena @ Bharti [(2011) 3 SCC 545], the Apex Court held that in view of Section 114(f) of Evidence Act read with Section 27 of General Clauses Act, there is a presumption that the addressee has received "
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "fd125104a0fd466ca95e1ede01a1135f_48",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nHowever, the presumption is rebuttable on a consideration of evidence of impeccable character."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "9cc4bb8ba6d842609c15de588ea3fbfb_49",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "[2024:RJ-JP:11523] (6 of 10) [CRLR-858/2005]\n13."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "383ad4892ca94205b2a87feff0e7c186_50",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It is also a settled law that the burden to rebut the presumption lies on the party challenging the factum of service."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "d59342c4b1464416b1bb4592b29af2db_51",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In the instant case, the petitioner has not challenged the factum of service."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "692ef7efcd6541bdb094b76a86945540_52",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The registered postal receipt (Exhibit P13) shows that the said report was sent to the petitioner's address and in absence of any specific defence the Court may presume that the accused has received the report."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "444b91aa1c6c42bb94cc081314efff0a_53",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The Courts below, in their judgments, have dealt with the issue in detail."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "326030fcd97546c0b84466c5016d9caa_54",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Further, the accused neither raised any objection in the trial nor attempted to get sample analysed through the Court from the central laboratory."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "8f5735aba02e4b4282c2b10740fdf665_55",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Therefore, the arguments raised by learned counsel for the accused-petitioner that the petitioner did not receive a public analyst report are without any substance."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "c87d841d971f4d3496d9845872779afd_56",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Accordingly, I do not find any perversity and illegality in the impugned order convicting the accused- petitioner under section 7/16 of the Act of 2006."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "9224ed0dd1dc4f2db47d9f785f59275a_57",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "14. The alternative plea for reduction of sentence was analysed in the latest pronouncement rendered in the matter of M/S A.K. Sarkar & Co. & Anr. Vs. The State of West Bengal (Special Leave Petition (Criminal) No.6095/2018) dated 07.03.202"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "185145f979554b71b0bfd043617905aa_58",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": ", the Apex Court held as under:-\n\"All the same, the above provision does not prohibit this Court, to award a lesser punishment in a befitting case, when this Court is of the opinion that a lesser punishment [2024:RJ-JP:11523] (7 of 10) [CRL"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "2b6f798c8ba746718234f3c38afcdbb8_59",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The prohibition contained in Article 20 of the Constitution of India is on subjecting a person to a higher punishment than which was applicable for that crime at the time of the commission of the crime."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "832b300fb8384118a9ffadac0654a2a6_60",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "There is no prohibition, for this Court to impose a lesser punishment which is now applicable for the same crime.\""
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "3b6fa25f5d4142e2929782c6d79ecc01_61",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "15. In the matter of T. Barai v. Henry Ah Hoe [(1983) 1 SCC 177], the Apex Court held that when an amendment is beneficial to the accused it can be applied even to cases pending in Courts where such a provision did not exist at the time of "
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "1b7a96eae7b94cff9030bea2f17b0c05_62",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The Apex Court further held that:-\nJamil vs State on 21 March, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/181648683/\n4 \"22."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "c30ee07240e74c8fae3c46d258d4427e_63",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It is only retroactive criminal legislation that is prohibited under Article 20(1)."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "0022e1d97d5c4ad9bc903ba9ff134a07_64",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nThe prohibition contained in Article 20(1) is that no person shall be convicted of any offence except for violation of a law in force at the time of the commission of the act charged as an offence prohibits nor shall he be subjected to a p"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "54e99da13e564d7fa365626f39c16eaa_65",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It is quite clear that insofar as the Central Amendment Act creates new offences or enhances punishment for a particular type of offence no person can be convicted by such ex post facto law nor can the enhanced punishment prescribed by the "
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "56518f4f3e1a49e58ba4ac24b68a2e48_66",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "But insofar as the Central Amendment Act reduces the punishment for an offence punishable under Section 16(1)(a) of the Act, there is no reason why the accused should not have the benefit of such reduced punishment."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "42bc1161953c4e3eb85572c55e7690c9_67",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The rule of beneficial construction requires that even ex post facto law of such a type should be applied to mitigate the rigour of the law."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "c84927b6a845421e84a8aeec890859b9_68",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The principle is based both on sound reason and common sense.\""
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "2beb63610b73401584b54b47ffea404b_69",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "16. In the aforesaid matter accused appellants were convicted under section 7/16 of the Prevention of Adulteration Act for simple imprisonment for a period of six months along with a fine of [2024:RJ-JP:11523] (8 of 10) [CRLR-858/2005] Rs.1"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "396d8697fbd242f2b32098c194b4d7d7_70",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The Apex Court, after taking into consideration the provisions of section 52 containing the punishment clause in the newly enacted Food Safety and Standards Act, converted the sentence of appellant No.2 from three months of simple imprisonm"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "bea6b14c65af4945921582ed30459ef6_71",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In the present case, the petitioner is convinced for the offence under Section 7/16 of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act for simple imprisonment of 6 months along with a fine of Rs.1000/-."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "07d64c81261d44ff8fdd6ee659898332_72",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It is alleged against the petitioner that he sold substandard milk."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "65cb5a9106704eba9187dc2b686b1b51_73",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "18. Indubitably the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act 1976 stands abrogated and replaced with the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "fc98a4c1564e4cb98de2f362a214b989_75",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The instant case falls under section (m) of the old Act."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "7ebf518e2f6142b79ae1049c168e9ed5_76",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In the Act of 2006, the definition of \"adulterant\" is provided under Section 3(1)(a), which reads as under:-\n(a) \"adulterant\" means any material which is or could be employed for making the food unsafe or sub-standard or mis-branded or cont"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b9a1f7e178ad402cb295cb8f4844912e_77",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In Section 51 of the Act of 2006, penalty for selling/ storing substandard articles is prescribed,\nwhich is as under:-\n\"51. Penalty for sub-standards food.-Any person who whether by himself or by any other person on his behalf [2024:RJ-JP:1"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b930592487504bab84be42af8481f49a_78",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Thus from the above provision, it is conspicuous that under the new act, only the penalty of a fine is stipulated therefore applying the doctrine articulated in the above-referred matters and also considering the fact that the crime itself "
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "96e586d35d0947c1b42ef8d404ebdff5_79",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The amount shall be deposited with the concerned Court within a period of three months from today."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "21669a5567e74c83ab37431bce1f7723_80",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "If the petitioner fails to deposit the aforesaid fine in the prescribed limit then the trial Court shall proceed to recover it, in accordance with law."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "71a13b880ba44f8f9c4f6cad58f32d4b_81",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "22. With the aforesaid directions, the revision petition is partially allowed."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "3ae517f2bc3c479ab66338e5aa8e1fcc_82",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "All other pending applications, if any, stand disposed of."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "cddb77d49ae946d79b03ffadf9acbdcb_83",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The record of the case is sent forthwith to the concerned Court to do the needful."
      }
    ],
